NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000243 "=head1 HOMEPAGE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000244 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000245 "Please visit the project's homepage at L<https://metacpan.org/release/List-Rank>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000246 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000247 "=head1 SOURCE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000248 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000249 "Source repository is at L<https://github.com/perlancar/perl-List-Rank>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000250 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000251 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000252 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000253 "L<Sort::Rank> also accomplishes the same thing, but by default it expects an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000254 "arrayref *of hashrefs* with key C<score> in each hashref. To process a list of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000255 "scalars, you need to supply a coderef to supply the scores. Another thing is,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000256 "the module does not provide a way to sort by a custom order."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000257 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000258 "=head1 AUTHOR"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000259 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000260 "perlancar <perlancar@cpan.org>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000261 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000262 "=head1 CONTRIBUTING"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000263 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000264 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000265 "To contribute, you can send patches by email/via RT, or send pull requests on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000266 "GitHub."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000267 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000268 "Most of the time, you don't need to build the distribution yourself. You can"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000269 "simply modify the code, then test via:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000270 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000271 " % prove -l"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000272 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000273 "If you want to build the distribution (e.g. to try to install it locally on your"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000274 "system), you can install L<Dist::Zilla>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000275 "L<Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::PERLANCAR>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000276 "L<Pod::Weaver::PluginBundle::Author::PERLANCAR>, and sometimes one or two other"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000277 "Dist::Zilla- and/or Pod::Weaver plugins. Any additional steps required beyond"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000278 "that are considered a bug and can be reported to me."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000279 ""
